{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105658-resisting-mage-magic-who-can-do-it-and-how","id":1105658,"title":"Resisting Mage Magic - who can do it and how?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-20T05:55:35-07:00","id":1105658,"title":"Resisting Mage Magic - who can do it and how?","content":"It has been years (decades, really) since I played Mage, and a friend is starting a cross genre game up. Everyone else is Vampire or Were, so I thought I'd throw a Mage in. The GM is suggesting what I think is a house rule that anyone can resist Magic if they know it's coming by making a Willpower check difficulty 8. To me, that seems to really hobble Mages, because Sphere dots are very expensive and Willpower is cheap, plus Spheres can't go over 5. It seems like if you let people throw 7 dice at something they're likely to get at least 1 8, while I only have say 3 or 4 dice to get successes with. <br /> <br /> What are the official ways to resist Magic, and who can do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6182-rando1000","name":"rando1000","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T06:10:33-07:00","id":1105662,"title":"","content":"Officially it's worse for you. Vamps resist with occult + willpower. I forget what garou do.<br /> <br /> Simple solution is to go for effects like hotshot or hands of death. You boost the force or efficiency of something mundanely lethal rather than directly trying to hex your opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T06:14:38-07:00","id":1105665,"title":"","content":"Do mortals use Willpower, officially?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6182-rando1000","name":"rando1000","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T06:19:51-07:00","id":1105666,"title":"","content":"I believe Mortals also use occult + willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T06:29:18-07:00","id":1105667,"title":"","content":"Man, that seems to make a Mage really weak, comparatively. I don't think we played that properly back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6182-rando1000","name":"rando1000","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T06:43:19-07:00","id":1105668,"title":"","content":"Well 5 willpower is generally speaking borderline superhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T06:48:09-07:00","id":1105670,"title":"","content":"That's a good point. Guess all I can do is give it a try and see how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6182-rando1000","name":"rando1000","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T07:12:26-07:00","id":1105673,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've managed to find the Night-Folk Counterspelling rules in the brick that is M20 (p. 546). It's time to clear up some misconceptions.<br /> <br /> First, no one uses Willpower for their Countermagic dice pool. They use Wits + <i>Occult</i>, all of them. Not Willpower.<br /> <br /> Willpower comes in, rather, as a <i>limiter</i> to a night-folk's countermagic dice pool. The dice pool cannot exceed the Willpower trait for Vampires (and most supernaturals, really). If the vamp has high Wits and Occult, but little Willpower, they can't do much. With Werewolves, their limit is either Gnosis or Rage (whichever is higher, though the Storyteller could easily make it whichever is lower, if they think the mages are too disadvantaged).<br /> <br /> Next, a Storyteller is fully within their rights to deny a night-folk character Countermagic entirely if they don't have any dots in Occult. In this case, the character wouldn't know where to begin resisting the mage's arcane might. Moreover, the Countermagic of a night-folk only works on spells targeting them directly. Aimed attacks like a laser bolt or enlightened martial arts can't be countered, nor can they negate Effects that would cause the character indirect harm (like weakened floorboards, or hacking the character's bank account).<br /> <br /> So in point of fact, the Countermagic other supernatural beings can bring to bear against mages is actually kind of limited.<br /> <br /> <br /> Further, I may offer my own interpretation of the rules that can even the playing field further in Mage's favor. Rather than the night-folk character just thinking about resisting the spell, they actually need to take the entire turn to <i>do something</i> that counters magic. It might be to cross oneself, brandish a holy symbol or protective amulet, fondle an iron object, make a hand sign, utter a prayer to Gaia or another being, etc. The character stops whatever they were doing, and uses their Occult knowledge to perform protective actions. Hence, why they can't begin to resist the magic unless they know enough about the Occult to know what they're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 06-20-2017, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T08:13:15-07:00","id":1105699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105658-resisting-mage-magic-who-can-do-it-and-how?p=1105673#post1105673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I've managed to find the Night-Folk Counterspelling rules in the brick that is M20 (p. 546). It's time to clear up some misconceptions.<br /> <br /> First, no one uses Willpower for their Countermagic dice pool. They use Wits + <i>Occult</i>, all of them. Not Willpower.<br /> <br /> Willpower comes in, rather, as a <i>limiter</i> to a night-folk's countermagic dice pool. The dice pool cannot exceed the Willpower trait for Vampires (and most supernaturals, really). If the vamp has high Wits and Occult, but little Willpower, they can't do much. With Werewolves, their limit is either Gnosis or Rage (whichever is higher, though the Storyteller could easily make it whichever is lower, if they think the mages are too disadvantaged).<br /> <br /> Next, a Storyteller is fully within their rights to deny a night-folk character Countermagic entirely if they don't have any dots in Occult. In this case, the character wouldn't know where to begin resisting the mage's arcane might. Moreover, the Countermagic of a night-folk only works on spells targeting them directly. Aimed attacks like a laser bolt or enlightened martial arts can't be countered, nor can they negate Effects that would cause the character indirect harm (like weakened floorboards, or hacking the character's bank account).<br /> <br /> So in point of fact, the Countermagic other supernatural beings can bring to bear against mages is actually kind of limited.<br /> <br /> <br /> Further, I may offer my own interpretation of the rules that can even the playing field further in Mage's favor. Rather than the night-folk character just thinking about resisting the spell, they actually need to take the entire turn to <i>do something</i> that counters magic. It might be to cross oneself, brandish a holy symbol or protective amulet, fondle an iron object, make a hand sign, utter a prayer to Gaia or another being, etc. The character stops whatever they were doing, and uses their Occult knowledge to perform protective actions. Hence, why they can't begin to resist the magic unless they know enough about the Occult to know what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either that or mages also get free counters.<br /> Currently all get free counters against anything affecting them directly, except for mages, they need an action to use countermagick (albeit they can counter anything in which they have the spheres at 1).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:07:55-07:00","id":1105723,"title":"","content":"What about a Tremere's Rego Magica?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:21:33-07:00","id":1105753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lordmagnusen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105658-resisting-mage-magic-who-can-do-it-and-how?p=1105723#post1105723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a Tremere's Rego Magica?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Perdo Magica? Because a quick search of the White Wolf wiki says that Rego Magica just makes new Paths, and it's Perdo that counters magic.<br /> <br /> Whatever. Thaumaturgical Countermagic.<br /> <br /> It works the way it works. Your rating gives you countermagic dice...against blood sorcery. According to V20, Thaumaturgical Countermagic works at half effectiveness against non-Thaumaturgy Disciplines (Necromancy, Ahku, etc.), and is &quot;completely ineffective against non-vampiric magics and powers&quot; (V20 Core, p. 228).<br /> <br /> So, apparently, it does nothing against Mages. At least according to V20. Unless the Storyteller says otherwise, it's useless. Even if we allowed it (which honestly seems more costly for the vampire PC than just using their Wits + Occult), I would personally still make it half as effective against Mage magick, with the possible exception of Hermetic magick (since Thaumaturgy and the Hermetic Arts are based on the same occult principles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:51:40-07:00","id":1105765,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry, Perdo. And I didn't know it was only against blood sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T18:57:17-07:00","id":1105908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105658-resisting-mage-magic-who-can-do-it-and-how?p=1105673#post1105673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I've managed to find the Night-Folk Counterspelling rules in the brick that is M20 (p. 546). It's time to clear up some misconceptions.<br /> <br /> First, no one uses Willpower for their Countermagic dice pool. They use Wits + <i>Occult</i>, all of them. Not Willpower.<br /> <br /> Willpower comes in, rather, as a <i>limiter</i> to a night-folk's countermagic dice pool. The dice pool cannot exceed the Willpower trait for Vampires (and most supernaturals, really). If the vamp has high Wits and Occult, but little Willpower, they can't do much. With Werewolves, their limit is either Gnosis or Rage (whichever is higher, though the Storyteller could easily make it whichever is lower, if they think the mages are too disadvantaged).<br /> <br /> Next, a Storyteller is fully within their rights to deny a night-folk character Countermagic entirely if they don't have any dots in Occult. In this case, the character wouldn't know where to begin resisting the mage's arcane might. Moreover, the Countermagic of a night-folk only works on spells targeting them directly. Aimed attacks like a laser bolt or enlightened martial arts can't be countered, nor can they negate Effects that would cause the character indirect harm (like weakened floorboards, or hacking the character's bank account).<br /> <br /> So in point of fact, the Countermagic other supernatural beings can bring to bear against mages is actually kind of limited.<br /> <br /> <br /> Further, I may offer my own interpretation of the rules that can even the playing field further in Mage's favor. Rather than the night-folk character just thinking about resisting the spell, they actually need to take the entire turn to <i>do something</i> that counters magic. It might be to cross oneself, brandish a holy symbol or protective amulet, fondle an iron object, make a hand sign, utter a prayer to Gaia or another being, etc. The character stops whatever they were doing, and uses their Occult knowledge to perform protective actions. Hence, why they can't begin to resist the magic unless they know enough about the Occult to know what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also require, and it's suggested in M20, that the character countering the True Magick effect needs to have some Thaumaturgy path or equivalent power in order for the supernatural creature in question to be able to roll counter magick at all. Occult knowledge is not enough, you need to know magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T00:46:21-07:00","id":1105975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105658-resisting-mage-magic-who-can-do-it-and-how?p=1105908#post1105908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also require, and it's suggested in M20, that the character countering the True Magick effect needs to have some Thaumaturgy path or equivalent power in order for the supernatural creature in question to be able to roll counter magick at all. Occult knowledge is not enough, you need to know magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it is fine if the target in question knows some related power.<br /> For example a Ventrue can counter Mind magick because he knows Dominate and/or Presence.<br /> He can counter pattern attacks like Rip the undead body because of his knowledge of Fortitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}